sw: LOK lists the body's paragraphs and the cursor's among them

A LOK client's screen reader gets one paragraph at a time: the a11y
events name only the paragraph that holds the caret, so "read to the
end" stops at that paragraph's last word, and a move to another
paragraph replaces the text instead of moving a caret through it.
getCommandValues gains ".uno:ElyReading": the expanded text of each
laid-out body paragraph in document order, and "caret", the index of
the cursor's among them. A cursor in a footnote, header or frame, or
text being typed into a shape, gets no "caret": those do not flow into
the body.

